Steps in DNA fingerprinting:
(i) Isolation of DNA;
(ii) digestion of the DNA by a restriction endonuclease enzyme;
(iii) separation of the DNA fragments by electrophoresis;
(iv) transfer of the separated fragments to a synthetic membrane, such as nitrocellulose or nylon;
(v) hybridisation using a labelled VNTR probe;
(vi) detection of the hybridised DNA fragments by autoradiography.

